<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ludwig Roselius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1874–1943</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ludwig Roselius (1874–1943) was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremen">Bremen</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> merchant who founded Kaffee HAG in 1906 to sell the first commercially successful decaffeinated coffee, using a process he had patented. He also financed the Böttcherstrasse in Bremen, a street of Expressionist buildings built in the 1920s and 1930s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ludwig-roselius.jpg" alt="Ludwig Roselius" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nicola Perscheid · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ludwig_Roselius_by_Nicola_Perscheid_c1905.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
